        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0bc1415a-8ce5-5a39-88cb-a590719e3cbb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nguyễn Văn Trỗi, Henry Cabot Lodge Jr., Robert McNamara\n- Places: South Vietnam, Massachusetts\n- Roles: United States Secretary of Defense, ambassador, United States Senator\n- Topics: assassination attempt, capture, diplomatic visit\n\nFacts:\n- In May 1963, Nguyễn Văn Trỗi was captured by South Vietnamese forces while trying to assassinate United States Secretary of Defense Robert McNamara and future ambassador Henry Cabot Lodge Jr. during their visit to South Vietnam.\n- Henry Cabot Lodge Jr. was born on July 5, 1902, and died on February 27, 1985.\n- Henry Cabot Lodge Jr., sometimes called Henry Cabot Lodge II, was a Republican United States Senator from Massachusetts and a United States ambassador.",
